Third-party software in the seagoat-worker binary
==================================================

The binary is built with microsandbox's `embed-binaries` feature, so it carries two prebuilt
programs as a compressed archive and unpacks them into $MSB_HOME on first run. Everything
else in it is statically linked Rust.

Running the binary yourself carries no obligations. Handing the binary to anyone else does:
ship this file with it, plus the license texts and the source for the two GPL/LGPL parts
below (a link to the exact upstream commit is the usual way to offer the source).

Embedded runtime (microsandbox 0.7.8)
-------------------------------------

msb 0.7.8
  License: Apache-2.0
  Source:  https://github.com/superradcompany/microsandbox/tree/v0.7.8

libkrunfw 5.6.1, microsandbox's fork, vendored at vendor/libkrunfw in the tag above
  License: LGPL-2.1-only (library code); GPL-2.0-only (the kernel and its patches)
  Source:  https://github.com/superradcompany/libkrunfw/tree/21f169f7e94798c8916315f8ac6f5999d5b88566
  The fork's README states that the library only stores the kernel and is not a derivative
  work of it, so programs linking it need not be GPL or LGPL. It is a separate file loaded at
  run time, so it can be swapped for another build, as the LGPL asks.

Linux 6.12.111, inside libkrunfw
  License: GPL-2.0-only
  Source:  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/linux-6.12.111.tar.xz
           plus the patches/ directory of the libkrunfw commit above

Statically linked Rust crates
-----------------------------

All are permissive except option-ext (MPL-2.0: file-level copyleft, met by using it
unmodified) and webpki-roots (CDLA-Permissive-2.0, Mozilla's root certificate data).
Regenerate after changing Cargo.lock, from tools/worker/:

  cargo tree -e normal --prefix none -f '{p}|{l}' | sed 's/ (\*)//; s/ (proc-macro)//' \
    | grep -v '^seagoat-worker' | sort -u | tr '|' '\t'

